  "query_preview": "..\n(Tonight through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1110 PM CDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nAnother calm overnight period is progressing across the Mid-South\nwith temperatures currently spanning the upper 70s to low 80s.\nThere is some ongoing convection over Middle TN along a lingering\nboundary, however, this activity is expected to stay to the east\nof the Mid-South. Otherwise, a rinse and repeat forecast is on\ntap for Wednesday with temperatures returning to the mid to upper\n90s across the area. With the well above-normal temperatures and\ndew points lingering in the mid 70s, heat index values will\nlikely approach to exceed 105 across much of the area. For this\nreason, a Heat Advisory will be in effect for Wednesday and\ncontinue through at least Thursday and Friday. Outside of the\nongoing, extreme heat, there will be a series of weak shortwaves\nthat swing through the Ohio River Valley Wednesday afternoon into\nThursday morning. Some of the 00Z guidance wants to have some\ndiurnally-driven, afternoon thunderstorms across north\nMississippi Wednesday afternoon, but given that this is a\nrelatively new trend, opted against any meaningful mention in our\nPoPs. In addition, one of the more potent shortwaves could bring\nthe potential for strong to severe thunderstorms to our north and\neast, but the vast majority of guidance keeps any activity\nassociated with this well to our east. The forecast will carry\nsome small PoPs (< 20%) mainly along the TN River Wednesday\nevening into the overnight hours for this reason, but again think\nthe better chances remain outside of the Mid-South.\n\nBy Friday, an upper-level ridge will continue to build over the\nregion with little to no relief expected until at least next\nweek. Latest NBM guidance has most of the Mid-South reaching the\nupper 90s by Friday, with temperatures increasing further by\nSaturday through Monday with highs peaking in the low 100s for\nmany. Latest LREF guidance through this same time period has\ngenerally a 40% to 60% chance of exceeding 100 degrees along and\nwest of the MS River on Friday, with these probabilities\nincreasing to the 60% to 80% range by Saturday. Guidance does\nbegin to become more spread by next Tuesday onward as the ridge\nbegins to break down. Despite the spread, conditions still look\nvery warm with unseasonably warm temperatures. As such,\nadditional heat headlines will likely be needed into the upcoming\nweekend and early next week. For those looking for temporary\nrelief, you may need to look somewhere else outside of the Mid-\nSouth for the next seven days.",
